      "title": "Everyone stops for the show. Almost nobody knows what they were actually looking at.\n\nThe Prague Astronomical Clock has been marking the hours since 1410, commissioned not just to tell time but to map the cosmos and announce that Prague belonged among Europe's great cities.\n\nThese six slides take you inside it: the clockmaker and astronomer who built it, how to read its three distinct faces, the mechanics behind the hourly Apostle procession, the famous blinding legend (and why historians say it almost certainly never happened), the wartime shelling that nearly ended it, and what the daily crowd on Old Town Square says about what the clock still means to Prague.\n\nHave you watched the procession in person?\n\nSave this for your next visit to Old Town Square and follow @praguetravelers for more of Prague told properly.",
